    {"v":"fcR_p3KKLMk","s":2493.12,"e":2494.08,"line":"Take the bus.","note":"Sheldon can’t drive, so he asks: How do I get to work? His friend says: Take the bus. Sheldon doesn’t like buses: they have no seat belts.","around":[[2490.16,2491.44,"Good night, Sheldon."],[2491.44,2493.12,"But how am I going to get to work?"],[2494.08,2495.36,"I can’t take the bus anymore."],[2495.36,2499.76,"They don’t have seat belts, and they won’t let you lash yourself to the seat with bungee cords."]]},
    {"v":"cey7PzQlDzs","s":2349.44,"e":2350,"line":"Stop the bus.","note":"Carl is on a bus. He sees a woman in trouble on the street and shouts to the driver: Stop the bus!","around":[[2330.8,2332.48,"Nice to meet you, Carl."],[2333.12,2334.08,"Take care."],[2350.16,2351.76,"That woman’s getting robbed."],[2352.32,2354,"That’s not a chance."]]},
